\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{frap}
\title{Label transport and topology}

\p{A sequence of puzzle moves may return pieces to their positions while
changing their orientations; the [cycle criterion](frap-000U) computes
that return map. Transporting labels between neighboring simplices is
another construction. Izmestiev and Joswig study it through projectivities,
coloring obstructions and branched coverings
\citet{Sections 2.1--2.3}{izmestiev2002branched}.}

\p{Their complete unfolding of the tetrahedron boundary is a torus
\citet{Section 2.3.3, Figure 3}{izmestiev2002branched}.
This example motivates a study of how local label transport records
global topology. Comparing simplex projectivities with puzzle transport
would require a map between the constructions and an argument that it
preserves the relevant data; no such identification is assumed here.}
